{
  "_doc": "Tier-3 roadside motel on Route 9 south of Pell's Crossing (region D6, feature timberline_motel). Front (+Z) faces the highway. Route: the lot (office barricaded, ground-floor rooms sealed) -> stairs to the upper walkway (STAY OFF WALKWAY; creaky boards wake Sallow, the trucker from 7) -> the housekeeper's cart outside 8: the master key -> room 8 -> the guests' route through the bathroom walls 8 -> 7 (soft floor drops into the keener's room 3) -> 6 (the Bells' bear trap at the hole; R. Bell's note wakes the Bells) -> 5, where the tub went through the floor -> drop into room 1 (the Hadleys), unbolt its door -> round the back to the guest laundry (ambush: Walt and the guests) -> the master key opens the door through to June's stair hall (gate) -> up to June's apartment: her register ('please knock first') -> her bedroom: Walt's shotgun wired to the door, June guarding the safe (loot, master key) -> back down, the master key opens the stair door into the office -> unbolt the office side door. Built as a straight two-storey strip (24 x 9) with the office block at the east end: an L would put the lot inside the building's interior probe and needs multi-rect roofs. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
