      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Walt and June Pruett ran the Timberline on Route 9 since 1961: eight rooms over two floors, the office with their apartment above it, the guest laundry and the ice machine. When the Guard closed the road at Cordon the motel filled with stranded motorists. Room 7 - a trucker named Sallow - coughed for two nights and then his door was open and there was blood on the walkway. The guests upstairs knocked through their bathroom walls from 8 to 5 so nobody had to walk past him again; the Ortiz boy fell through the floor of 5 when the tub went. Walt went to see about the laundry and did not come back. June pushed the soda machine against the office doors, locked the door to her stairs and went up with the safe and Walt's shotgun. The housekeeper's master keys are still on her cart outside room 8.",
